\description{
Compute predictive performance measures on the same data used to fit the
model. This is the simplest entry point when you want density scores
(\code{elpd}) and optional distributional or point-prediction metrics in
one call.

In-sample \code{elpd} sums the expected log pointwise predictive density (ELPD)
over the training observations. Because the model has already seen these
data, in-sample scores are \strong{optimistically biased} for predicting future
or otherwise unseen observations. For out-of-sample performance, use
\code{\link[=loo_pred_measure]{loo_pred_measure()}}, \code{\link[=kfold_pred_measure]{kfold_pred_measure()}}, or \code{\link[=test_pred_measure]{test_pred_measure()}}
instead; see Vehtari's
\href{https://users.aalto.fi/~ave/CV-FAQ.html}{Cross-validation FAQ} (Section 4).
}
